</element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig position="float" id="F1" fig-type="figure"><label>Fig. (1)</label><caption><p>An operating and assisting surgeon using Zero Gravity (ZG) during an endovascular aneurysm repair procedure. </p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CCR-21-1-E1573403X304828_F1" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F2" fig-type="figure"><label>Fig. (2)</label><caption><p>The Radiation Shielding System (RSS) - a novel robotic radiation shielding system that provides full-body protection to all medical personnel in the catheterization laboratory during fluoroscopy-guided procedures by encapsulating the imaging beam and blocking the scattered radiation at its origin. </p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CCR-21-1-E1573403X304828_F2" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F3" fig-type="figure"><label>Fig. (3)</label><caption><p>The CorPath GRX system. (<bold>A</bold> and <bold>B</bold>) Overview of the CorPath GRX system in the catheterization laboratory. (<bold>C</bold>) A single-use cassette connected with a vascular access sheath. (<bold>D</bold>) Control console. a Turbo button. b Balloon/stent catheter joystick. c Guidewire joystick. d Guide catheter joystick. e Emergency stop button. (<bold>E</bold>) An operator remotely controls the movement of PCI devices, sitting down in a radiation-shielded cockpit. </p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CCR-21-1-E1573403X304828_F3" position="float"/></fig></floats-group></article>